    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d230-a4-a7">

                <pb facs="0579" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg493"/>

                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Consulate of
                            Belgium and the Netherlands</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-12-12"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 12,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your excellency’s dispatch or yesterday, by which I received the mournful
                    intelligence of the sudden and unexpected demise of His Majesty King Kamehamaha
                    V.</p>
                <p>I beg to assure your excellency of the profound feelings of sympathy and
                    condolence with the royal family and the Hawaiian nation with which this sad
                    event has filled me, and have the honor to remain your excellency’s most
                    obedient, humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. BANNING.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">F. W. Hutchison</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs, &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
